---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Do we need to replace our existing software before automating processes?",
    answer:
      "Not necessarily. Many automation projects connect existing systems through APIs, webhooks, scheduled processes or other integration methods where those systems support them.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can automation work between different systems?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Cross-system automation is often one of the main opportunities, provided the systems expose suitable integration or data-access capabilities.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can approvals remain manual?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Automation can route and prepare the work while keeping important approvals or judgement-based decisions with people.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKP automate a process currently managed through spreadsheets?",
    answer:
      "Potentially. We first review how the spreadsheet is being used and determine whether the process should be automated around it or moved into a more structured system.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "How do you identify what should be automated?",
    answer:
      "Good candidates are usually repetitive, rule-based processes involving predictable inputs, hand-offs, notifications, data entry or recurring documents.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does automation require AI?",
    answer:
      "No. Many valuable business automations are deterministic workflows based on clear rules. AI is useful only where the process genuinely benefits from interpretation, classification or generation.",
  },
];
---

<section class="automation-faq">
  <div class="site-container automation-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Business automation FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before automating the process.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="automation-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .automation-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .automation-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .automation-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .automation-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .automation-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .automation-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .automation-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .automation-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .automation-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
